    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "Depiction of the two forms of the god Quetzalcoatl on folio 19 of Codex Laud, a pre-Hispanic Mexican manuscript possibly made in the 15th century. His form as the feathered serpent, celestial deity, is depicted at the left, and his form as the god of the wind Ehecatl is seen at the right, with his characteristic completely black skin, beard and red mask.",
